      <p class="eyebrow">About</p>
      <h1>I like difficult systems and useful questions.</h1>
      <p class="hero-dek">I’m Nanda Raghunathan. I’ve worked in the tech industry for over two decades, and I’m the person behind NandLabs.</p>
      <div class="prose compact">
        <p>My work has moved between distributed systems, product engineering, and organizational leadership. This site is where I explore the ideas and questions that emerged along the way, in my own voice.</p>
        <p>NandLabs is where I make the rest of the thinking visible: technical notes, business ideas, curated links, and experiments that may not fit neatly into a job description.</p>
        <p>I’m interested in how good systems earn trust, how engineering organizations keep their judgment as they grow, and how small experiments can expose big assumptions.</p>
      </div>
